{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead","id":540495,"title":"Raising the dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T20:59:38-07:00","id":540495,"title":"Raising the dead","content":"In the VtM game I am running a PC lost someone close to them and obsessively wants to bring them back to life. Now they don't really know the various game lines well but are going to look into every route to find a way to do it. Game by game what is the closest that can be achieved? It's a bit late for embracing by the way.<br /> <br /> Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Wraith, Changeling, Mummy, Demon, Hunter. I already know Changeling and Hunter are right out the window lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:20:53-07:00","id":540538,"title":"","content":"Wraith, particularly Risen (ala the Crow)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/250/The-Risen?it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/250.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/250/The-Risen?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> The Risen - White Wolf | Wraith: The Oblivion | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/250/The-Risen?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/250/The-Risen?it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Risen - The Told You There Was No Coming Back Vincent screamed when he saw us - me - again. After killing me, he'd expected me </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or Mummy, which is more easily integrated into another game, but harder for the PC to influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1251/Mummy-The-Resurrection?term=mummy+&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/1251.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1251/Mummy-The-Resurrection?term=mummy+&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> Mummy: The Resurrection - White Wolf | Mummy: The Resurrection | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1251/Mummy-The-Resurrection?term=mummy+&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1251/Mummy-The-Resurrection?term=mummy+&amp;it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Mummy: The Resurrection - Osiris Awakens. The Undying Rise Anew Given the choice of life or death, we choose to live again as soldiers of Osiris. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:43:19-07:00","id":540578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...raising the dead can be..troubling, its easier for mages..sort of.... complicated. but like stephen king thought us &quot;Dead is better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> and science helps too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:41:05-07:00","id":540602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=540578#post540578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/yJofMi88aB0?t=34</a><br /> <br /> ...raising the dead can be..troubling, its easier for mages..sort of.... complicated. but like stephen king thought us &quot;Dead is better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> and science helps too</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. If you want to go the 'Pet Cemetary / Monkey Paw' route, then just hit up the Giovanni. I'm sure they could whip something up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:58:26-07:00","id":540780,"title":"","content":"If its too late for the Embrace, then its too late for most methods. As far as I know, only one character has ever (canonically) been brought back, after their corpse had cooled - and that was Osiris. It took a pair of highly skilled mages working together to pull that off . . . and arguably he didn't come back right. Plus, the secret of how they did that is lost - there's one ancient mummy who <i>might</i> have witnessed the ritual, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Really, their only hope is that the deceased had strong passions, and unfinished business. That would allow them to hang around as a wraith, and maybe someday become a Risen (although that's more zombie than resurrection). It might take some retconning into your story to pull it off, but since most rookie wraiths can't affect anything on the living side of the Shroud, that should be doable. <br /> <br /> Or, if they're Asian, they could come back as a kuei-jin (<b>Kindred of the East</b>) . . . although that's not really a fate most people would want for a friend or loved one. It means that they've been the &quot;guest&quot; of the demon lords of the East, and subject to all the torments of Yomi. And now they're a fugitive from hell, desperately trying to find a way to avoid going back.<br /> <br /> But . . .that's kind of it. Even in the World of Darkness, the dead usually stay dead. You might be able to tell some good stories, though, about the PC learning to cope with his loss. Or about him going mad with grief, turning to increasingly dark and unholy figures in desperation, and eventually degenerating into a (real) monster (hey, it <i>is</i> still the World of Darkness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T03:54:02-07:00","id":540882,"title":"","content":"There are a number of ways it <i>could</i> happen across the official game lines but they're all difficult, dangerous, and stand a fair chance of going horribly wrong. Success could provide for good drama as well as failure and increasingly desperate attempts.<br /> <br /> You could also borrow from outside sources, like the posthumous Embrace in <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> which can work up to a week if the victim had ever tasted a vampire's blood and is <i>almost</i> without unusual side effects. Bringing that into <b>Masquerade</b> I'd suggest including some issues, like a need for a ritual (and a big favour to the Giovanni) and/or some odd Flaws that result like the late-Embraced character needing more blood to rise.<br /> <br /> I suppose the question, best discussed with the player, is what would be most interesting? Failure and despair, a hard-won success like a descent into the underworld, or a relatively easy revival with consequences to follow, for the vampire or the subject or both? (See <b>Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell</b> for a great current example of the latter.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:49:56-07:00","id":541085,"title":"","content":"The Player Character in question is not particularly a scholar of the occult and I am certain anything he does is going to lead to a walking corpse with murderous intent. Just wanted to know where to start reading up depending on which direction he takes. (Studying Egyptian occult, demon pacts, mortis, wraiths, mage magic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:53:54-07:00","id":541205,"title":"","content":"All of these seem good and legit.<br /> <br /> Demonic entities aren't know from bringing people back, but they probably will tell the character otherwise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Wraiths are a must for any would be necromancer, and should probably study diverse forms of occult.<br /> <br /> Mages have some real mojo to raise the dead (there's even an example of how to do it in M20, and that's not the only one), but it usually requires the character to be recently dead.<br /> Oh, and it's heavily Paradoxical.<br /> <br /> If the victim have left a Wraith (or a Spectre), then the spirit could be given a body with mage magic, also with vampiric necromancy (I think), and I don't know any other way. In the Spectre case, &quot;walking corpse with murderous intent&quot; it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:58:11-07:00","id":541336,"title":"","content":"ok..things i have come up with to bring someone back to life<br /> <br /> One: Be a risen, use make up, listen to the cure, seek for vengeance<br /> Two: Mage way (paradox) or make him a frankenstein thing, keeping the exact memories of himself but in a different body..or alter the memories so he and any witness forget that he died./Science &quot;Clone Him and use machinery to mimick his personality&quot;<br /> Three: Demons using all their lores combined...But this might end up good or badly (Oh my god, a human revived through pure torment......someone has to writte about this)<br /> Four: Posession, make a demon possess the dead host, there you go..Improved Eddy with firebreath and a nihilist attitude","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:15:14-07:00","id":541413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=540780#post540780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, if they're Asian, they could come back as a kuei-jin (<b>Kindred of the East</b>) . . . although that's not really a fate most people would want for a friend or loved one. It means that they've been the &quot;guest&quot; of the demon lords of the East, and subject to all the torments of Yomi. And now they're a fugitive from hell, desperately trying to find a way to avoid going back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half of them, anyway. Only the vigor soul, aka the po, goes to hell. The cloud soul stays around the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:00:34-07:00","id":541536,"title":"","content":"The NWoD Promethean game suggests other possibilities for bringing someone back to... life-ish via science, alchemy, and what have you. I'd say using <i>Frankenstein</i> as a guidebook could lead to some interesting stories. There's also the option of going the delusional route, and having the PC only <b>think</b> the loved one has been brought back.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I'd say that any method used to resurrect the dead other than actual divine intervention should lead to lots of unpleasantness for the person raised, the person doing the raising, and innocent bystanders in their lives. Whether the result is a zombie, a patchwork being with no true identity, an exceedingly solid ghost, another kind of vampire, or a demonically-animated doppelganger, it should be at least as tortuous for the person breaking all the laws of nature as dealing with his grief would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:48:17-07:00","id":542374,"title":"","content":"I agree with Craig - this is really something you need to discuss with the player (possibly the entire group). Decide (at least vaguely) what direction you want to go in, and how big a part of your game this should be. That way you can work up some interesting (side) adventures &amp; npcs, he gets to play out the character's obsession, and the other players aren't crowded out. Do it right, and this'll transcend a mere dungeon crawl - this could end up a work of art.<br /> <br /> Plus, you have a decision to make. Unless the dead person's soul is still hanging around, as a wraith/spectre, or in one of the pseudo-afterlives in an Umbral realm. . . .its not going to be possible to bring them back. Not without the direct intervention of God, or possibly one of the Oracles (who have magic that transcend the <i>Mage</i> game). So if (s)he's truly &quot;moved on&quot;, nothing is going to be able to bring them back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=541085#post541085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Player Character in question is not particularly a scholar of the occult and I am certain anything he does is going to lead to a walking corpse with murderous intent. Just wanted to know where to start reading up depending on which direction he takes. (Studying Egyptian occult, demon pacts, mortis, wraiths, mage magic)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good - that's very World of Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Reading <b>Mage</b> - unless you're planning a full blown crossover (which can be cool) - isn't really going to be productive. The <i>Mage </i>rules get very &quot;meta&quot;, very quickly, which gets away from what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Instead, if your group wants to pursue the mage angle, you should probably pick a couple of (real world) styles, and read up on them. Each mage has a sort of &quot;theme&quot; to their magic: super scientist, voodoo priest, faith healer . . . and they can use their &quot;Quintessence&quot; (read &quot;Blood Pool&quot;) to achieve &quot;impossible&quot; effects - <i>in that style</i>. A mad scientist probably can't summon an angel, but might be able to pull a Frankenstein. Or the holy man on the mountain - he isn't going to have robot legions, but might be able to talk directly to God.<br /> <br /> So if you're thinking of bringing in a mage or two (for a while), its really more important to get the &quot;feel&quot; of their style of magic down, and worry less about the actual mechanics. Mage magic (even the &quot;scientific&quot; type) depends heavily on atmosphere and belief, so you really want to get the trappings of the style right (which, incidentally, will help make it more memorable for the group, too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 06-08-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T01:22:45-07:00","id":542381,"title":"","content":"Oh, and if you're looking for a canon example of how badly a resurrection can go wrong, take a look at the Bane Mummies (from <b>Mummy</b>, obvioiusly). Back when Set and Horus were feuding over Egypt, Set decided his vampiric Followers weren't enough - he wanted his own mummies, too. So he brought in some dark mages . . .<br /> <br /> And the result was horrific. Seven loyal minions died . . . seven abominations came back. <i>Things</i> that had the memories of the dead, but not their souls. Oh, sure the personality was <i>sort of </i>right - but ultimately it was only a cruel parody. These &quot;Bane Mummies&quot; were loyal only to hell, and bound to the cause of universal destruction.<br /> <br /> And yet, they still had the signature power of mummies - the ability to resurrect themselves. Stabbed, shot, burned, devoured by werecrocodiles . . . sooner or later, they would always rise again.<br /> <br /> So if you want to really torture the PC, you might consider having their loved one &quot;return&quot; as a Bane Mummy. Their friend, but not - and a horrific monster, to boot. And no matter what they do, the PC will never be able to make it right. The damage is done, and this <i>creature</i>, which looks and talks just like the deceased, is loose on the world. And yet it makes a mockery of everything the lost loved one stood for. Even if the PC breaks down, and kills it, it just <i>won't stay dead</i>.<br /> <br /> Could be an interesting way to bring a recurring villain into the series, if you're interested. I'd suggest drawing that out a bit, though, to get the most out of the &quot;pure&quot; grief, first. It'll make the new Bane Mummy more horrific<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i> Incidentally, not all mummies (true or Bane) are Egyptian. Horus &quot;mass produced' them (creating maybe 100) to fight Set, resulting in a large cultural block of Egyptian ones, but the &quot;Great Rite&quot; has been independently developed in most cultures that practice mummification. So there are Incan mummies, Chinese mummies . . . many of whom don't like their Egyptian &quot;cousins&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:03:57-07:00","id":543928,"title":"","content":"I had something similar happen in a Mage chronicle a decade and change ago... But it was the entire cabal. A close associate was killed horribly right in front of them during a battle when all but one of them was helpless to do anything about it. The player of the one character dropped out of the game shortly afterwards and the other players really really wanted Edward back...<br /> <br /> It didn't completely dominate the game, but that desire did become major focus. Trying to figure out what to do become a passion. Followed shortly thereafter by collecting all the relevant &quot;plot coupons&quot; needed to make it happen. (Which I started placing here and there. But they had to figure them out. There was some backtracking and substitution.) It also involved them having to learn a lot about how each others' magic worked, how Edward's had worked, and how they could overlap. <br /> <br /> Ir was a lot of fun. They had to overcome a lot of problems to make it happen. For example. since the body was gone-gone, they had to acquire a new one... They ended up using the body of an opponent whose soul had almost entirely hollowed out during possession by a specter. They had to put the body into suspended animation and popped it into a Han Dynasty suit of jade burial armor to &quot;marinate&quot; it appropriately. (They had to make a fairly unpleasant deal with a vampire Prince to acquire the jade suit). It ended up working out that the body still had a little bit of soul left in it, which ended up not being as bad a thing as it could have been, as Edward's soul was somewhat damaged from being caught in a perpetual loop of reliving the horrific moment of his death in a little tiny Atrocity Realm. However, it did mean the Edward they got back was not entirely the Edward they had lost... E.g. Now Edward, who had been raised in a Euthanatos monastery with a pretty austere and terrible childhood, became a fan of watching (American) football games, during which he ate classic bar food. All of which was completely out of character. (That's a cute example. Not all of the results were cute at all.)<br /> <br /> One of the most interesting complications was that one of the PC's was pregnant and Edward was the father. That was, pre-death, different body Edward. That lead to some... adjustments... in the relationship after he was reincarnated/resurrected/(re)assembled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:36:46-07:00","id":547163,"title":"","content":"There are a few European (Greek?) mummies running around too. So in theory, it is possible.<br /> <br /> However, the person in question should be a wraith at least, because otherwise their soul would have passed on. Reviving someone without a soul is bound to cause all kinds of nastiness (although this is the World of Darkness, so this is probably exactly what you're intending, right?). But reanimating the dead flesh is probably the least difficult part. Even a Giovanni could do that (if he had the right paths of Necromancy). Reviving the body and restoring its corpse to an undecayed state is even possible. You could even summon *something* to dwell inside that body. <br /> <br /> In fact, you could have them bargaining with various different supernaturals to have various parts of the process performed one at a time. Step 1: reset the decay and preserve the body. Step 2: revive the body. Step 3: summon a spirit. Step 4: all hell breaks loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T03:36:37-07:00","id":549939,"title":"","content":"Why has not anyone mentioned the <i>Gurahl</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:41:23-07:00","id":550916,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about them, what kind of resurrection mojo do they have?. <br /> <br /> An Archmage with Entropy 8 it's pretty much the only thing I know that can raise the dead after any amount of time, even if the soul has been devoured by the Oblivion, and left no Wraith/Spectre. The only thing with rules, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:11:15-07:00","id":550933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=550916#post550916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about them, what kind of resurrection mojo do they have?.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is both a level 5 Rite and a Rank 5 Gift to being back the dead. The Rite can go back further, but is much, <b>much</b> more dangerous to use.<br /> <b>Gaia\u2019s Breath</b> (Level Five Gift)<br /> With this legendary Gift, the Gurahl may return a deceased shapeshifter to life. Bear herself teaches this Gift.<br /> <i>System:</i> The player spends one point each of permanent Gnosis and Willpower, then rolls Charisma + Occult (difficulty 6 + the number of hours since death). Success restores life to the target with one health level restored per success. A botch opens the corpse to possession by a powerful Bane. This Gift may be attempted once and only once on a single creature.<br /> <br /> <b>Rite of Fighting the Death Bear (Level Five)</b> - Whenever the Gurahl wishes to return the soul of a departed to it's body which has been dead too long for the use of the Gaia's Breath gift, he may employ this dangerous Rite to take back the spirit from the lands of the dead and bring it back to the world of the Living. The Gurahl must first rend the gauntlet where he makes the appropriate acts of chiminage, and summons the Death Bear, Mangi.<br /> <br /> The Gurahl engages the Bear in Combat. If Mangi is defeated he can enter the Death Bears realm and retrieve the soul. If the Gurahl is defeated he is cast from the umbra immediately. If the Gurahl dies in battle, the Death Bear may sometimes exchange the souls and return the soul as if the Rite had succeeded. The high price of this Rite makes it rare in use and it has only ever been used on other Gurahl. As with Gaia's Breath only one attempt may be used on any target, Ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:52:44-07:00","id":551285,"title":"","content":"I know that the Giovanni has a new Necromancy ritual from Lore of the Clans that allows you to embrace a person up to like a month after the actual death. Not a pretty solution but it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:41:14-07:00","id":552534,"title":"","content":"He seems to be pursuing the &quot;infernalism&quot; route","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:11:57-07:00","id":552582,"title":"","content":"Oh, <i>that'll </i>end well. <img src=\"http://www.4smileys.com/smileys/devil-smileys/devil_smiley_005.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:38:03-07:00","id":559862,"title":"","content":"For Mummy the Resurrection;<br /> Well if you are merciful ST (or sinister depends on the perspective) you can turn them in Amenti which forces your new character into 'good guy'.<br /> <br /> If you want to make them suffer more you can raise them as Asekh-Sen (Reaper). They are corrupted (both in soul and body) servants of Apepnu (Bane Mummies). So you can kick them in to plots of Apepnu as toys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6523-dzyhanas","name":"Dzyhanas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:57:06-07:00","id":559920,"title":"","content":"Hmm... just got a neat movie out of the Redbox called <i>Avenged</i>. A victim of a gang-rape/murder comes back from the dead, with something a bit meaner sharing her body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:24:17-07:00","id":562634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=549939#post549939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why has not anyone mentioned the <i>Gurahl</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>What the Gurahl do is true resurrection. I think what they want is people made by man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:53:24-07:00","id":564375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/540495-raising-the-dead?p=550916#post550916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Archmage with Entropy 8 it's pretty much the only thing I know that can raise the dead after any amount of time, even if the soul has been devoured by the Oblivion, and left no Wraith/Spectre. The only thing with rules, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably someone with Time 6 (or whatever rating it's been stretched out to in Revised/M20) would be able to reach back in time to before a person died and bring them forward into the present day. Depending on how time works in your game it might either change history or generate a divergent timeline in which said person suddenly disappears with no explanation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:05:31-07:00","id":564475,"title":"","content":"True, and in M20 with 5 it's enough. The paradox of such an act has to be staggering, though (albeit Entropy 8 isn't the panacea in that aspect).<br /> <br /> It's much easier to resurrect someone that has recently dead. That's true both for mages and Gurahl (and for other supernaturals too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-22-2015, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}